irectly.",remediation:"Run `coral-cli backend recovery-quarantine list` to inspect the continuation. Leave it retained for the owning recovery flow; do not repeat clear with the same coordinate."},recovery_quarantine_retry_in_progress:{userMessage:"A recovery retry is already in progress for that quarantine row.",remediation:"Wait for the coordinator to finish the retry, then run `coral-cli backend recovery-quarantine list`. Retry clear only if the row returns to the active state."},expansion_binary_corrupt:{userMessage:e=>`The installed binary for ${x(e,"name","this expansion")} could not be activated.`,remediation:e=>`Run 'coral-cli expansion unequip ${x(e,"name","<name>")}' before retrying 'coral-cli expansion equip ${x(e,"name","<name>")}'.`},installer_payload_invalid:{userMessage:"Expansion installer returned an invalid payload.",remediation:"Retry the command. If this persists, report the code because the installer response failed internal validation."},coordinator_record_unreadable:{userMessage:e=>`Coral cannot report ${x(e,"subject","expansion status")}: the coordinator discovery record at ${x(e,"path","<record-path>")} could not be read (${x(e,"detail","unknown")}). This does not mean no coordinator is running.`,remediation:e=>`Fix the permissions on ${x(e,"path","<record-path>")}, or delete it if its content is corrupt \u2014 a running coordinator never rewrites it, and a fresh one recreates it safely. Then run 'coral-cli backend start'; it attempts startup or handoff. Retrying this exact command re-reads the same file and will not resolve on its own.`,exitCode:75,observation:"not_observed"},coordinator_unreachable:{userMessage:e=>`Coral cannot report ${x(e,"subject","expansion status")}: the coordinator recorded itself at ${x(e,"path","<record-path>")} but did not answer (${x(e,"detail","unknown")}).`,remediation:e=>`Retry shortly in case the coordinator is only busy. If it persists, run 'ps -p ${x(e,"pid","<pid>")}' or check your process manager to see w